# post-M6 partition realignment — gate-test reclassification + corpus-gate path-list + dev-mode-manifest roots/always_loaded refresh

2026-04-29. Closes the LAST PRE-PUBLISH BLOCKER per dispatcher
recommendation analysis 2026-04-29 — three coherent surfaces, each
a "post-M6b.0 path move not fully propagated" instance.

Surface A — gate-test partition reclassification (M9 plan §7
finding #1). 12 gate-test files at framework/hands-off-lifecycle/
tests/test_AC_AG_*.py (5 files: 1_wrong_wd_dispatch +
2_method_enumerated_prompt + 3_stale_dispatch + 4_no_op_normal_use
+ 5_audit_log) + test_AC_BAG_*.py (7 files: 1_secret_commit +
2_blast_radius + 3_amend_in_subagent + 4_loam_amend_dry_run +
5_wrong_tree_write + 6_no_op_non_matching + 7_audit_log) sys.path-
probe into plugins/dev-sdlc/hooks/ (dev_only). Pre-fix they
classified dev_and_public via the broad framework/hands-off-
lifecycle/** glob; post-fix they classify dev_only via an explicit
glob entry that wins per partition-precedence rule #2 (dev_only
checked before dev_and_public). Synthesised public artefact no
longer carries gate-test files that depend on dropped plugin
modules.

Surface B — corpus_gate hook on-demand path-list update. framework/
hands-off-lifecycle/hooks/corpus_inline_session_start.py _ON_DEMAND
constant lines 135-139: first two entries rebased from docs/odd-
methodology.md + docs/odd-in-loam.md (pre-M6b.0 paths) to plugins/
dev-sdlc/docs/odd-methodology.md + plugins/dev-sdlc/docs/odd-in-
loam.md (post-M6b.0 plugin-tree paths). The hook's mode-partition
early-return (line 333-334 — mode != "dev-mode" no-ops) is the
graceful-skip mechanism for NORMAL-USE workspaces where the plugin
is dropped; no additional graceful-skip wiring needed.

Surface C — dev-mode-manifest.yaml roots: + always_loaded:
realignment (M1c-corrective plan §16 HSF#1). plugins/dev-sdlc/dev-
mode-manifest.yaml roots: block (lines 36-64) + always_loaded:
block (lines 78-110) referenced 15 top-level component dirs that
MOVED under framework/ post-M6b.0. Realignment shape:
  - 14 component refs rebased to framework/<comp>/ — cost-
    governance, hands-off-lifecycle, memory-system, objective-
    tracker, observability-aggregator, orchestrator, primary-
    persona, reversibility-primitive, safety-layer, scope-of-work,
    self-correction, self-upgrade, telegram-interface, workspace-
    bootstrap.
  - 1 component RENAME + REBASE — graceful-degradation/ → framework/
    dormancy/ (the component was renamed to dormancy/ pre-M6b.0;
    the manifest carried the old name forward). HSF#1 surfaced.
  - 1 component ADD — framework/workspace-sync/ — a missing
    component admission (workspace-sync was never in the manifest;
    original sub-plan F authoring's 15-component list predated
    the workspace-sync component and no subsequent amendment added
    it). HSF#2 surfaced.
  - tools/ → framework/tools/.
  - first-run-inventory.yaml → framework/first-run-inventory.yaml.
  - data/ STAYS top-level (workspace runtime telemetry, not a
    component source surface).
  - docs/ + CLAUDE.md + CLAUDE.dev.md + README.md STAY top-level.
  - dev_only: block NO EDITS (already realigned at M6c HSF#1 fix
    + M1c-corrective HSF#1 fix per HSF#5 finding).

AC surface (AC.PMR.1..PMR.7 + AC.PMR.S):

  - AC.PMR.1: 12 gate-test files classify dev_only via classify_path.
    Negative-control: non-gate test files in same dir continue
    dev_and_public.
  - AC.PMR.2: corpus_inline_session_start.py _ON_DEMAND first 2
    entries are plugins/dev-sdlc/docs/odd-{methodology,in-loam}.md;
    end-to-end SessionStart envelope drives main() and rendered
    on-demand block lists both plugin-relative paths.
  - AC.PMR.3: dev-mode-manifest roots: every entry resolves on disk;
    graceful-degradation/ → dormancy/ rename verified; framework/
    workspace-sync/ ADD verified.
  - AC.PMR.4: dev-mode-manifest always_loaded: every glob/path
    resolves to a non-empty match-set; data/ stays top-level;
    first-run-inventory.yaml rebased.
  - AC.PMR.5: compute_corpus_paths_required(workspace_root, "dev-
    mode") returns ≥10 paths, all of which exist on disk via the
    existing two-tier fall-through.
  - AC.PMR.6: corpus_gate sentinel state ∈ {"loaded", "partial"}
    post-realignment (NOT "missing"). The "loaded vs partial"
    branch depends on subset relationship between inline hook's
    static 3-path always-load and manifest-derived required set;
    AC asserts only that the degenerate "missing" state is gone.
  - AC.PMR.7: pre-existing tests pass — gate hook tests + corpus
    load tests + partition tests + 60 loam-mode tests.
  - AC.PMR.S: seal-diff invariant — 3 sealed components fence;
    edits land only under framework/hands-off-lifecycle/, plugins/
    dev-sdlc/, framework/tools/pos-publish-framework-only/, or
    universal admissions.

Method-level choices (builder's call per ODD §1.1):

  - D-build.PMR.1: Surface A entry shape — glob-with-pattern vs
    explicit 12-path list. Glob-with-pattern matches partition
    manifest's existing entry-shape precedent.
  - D-build.PMR.2: Surface C roots: style — per-component-glob
    (preserves granularity, matches publish-mode manifest pattern)
    vs bulk framework/** (loses surgical control).
  - D-build.PMR.3: workspace-sync/ ADD in-amendment vs deferred.
    In-amendment per scope-cohesion (single-source-of-truth pass).
  - D-build.PMR.4: AC.PMR.3+.4 test-file placement — plugins/dev-
    sdlc/tests/ (matches AC.PMR.S fence) vs plugins/dev-sdlc/tools/
    loam-mode/tests/ (co-locates with consumer).
  - D-build.PMR.5: Manifest-authoring commit ladder — separate
    docs(plans): for manifest yaml + feature commit for source/
    test (mirrors M9 + M1c-corrective precedent) vs single feature
    commit.

Out of scope (per plan §6):

  - 3 silent-swallow patterns in memory-system + 6 in orchestrator/
    supervisor.py (graceful-fallthrough-with-detection CDC
    retroactive audit; post-v0.1.0).
  - pos_orchestrator editable-install provisioning gap (HSF#3 from
    M1c-corrective; pre-existing; not pre-publish blocker).
  - Reorganising dev_only: block beyond workspace-sync ADD.
  - Adding NORMAL-USE-mode graceful-skip for missing plugin docs
    in corpus_inline_session_start.py (verified existing mode-
    partition is the skip).
  - Substitution-table extension (realigned paths are workspace-
    relative, not canonical-host).
  - Promoting data/ from always_loaded to its own root partition.
  - Anything not on Surface A / B / C.

BASELINE 699a391 (current HEAD post-M1c-corrective SHA backfill).
Each component's SEAL_COMMIT sidecar lands at the seal SHA via
`loam amend seal --scoped-sweep`. pos-publish-framework-only
admitted via universal_paths.prefixes (no per-component seal-test
sidecar — same shape M9 used; the structural surface is the
partition manifest YAML edit + 1 new test under tests/).

# M8-corrective — HC#4 byte-content rebaseline post-Apache-header insertion

2026-05-01. Foldback for M7-partition-fix HT-4 halt (HSF#1):
M8 commit `6bef03b` ("feat(public): M8 license-governance —
Apache headers on runtime .py + SECURITY.md tightening") inserted
a 14-line Apache-2.0 license header at the top of every runtime
.py file across 15 dev_and_public framework components per
AC.OSS.4, but did NOT perform the corresponding HC#4 retire-and-
rebaseline of the captured SHAs in HOL's
`test_d1_byte_content_match.py`. 13 of the test's 15 sample
files (all .py samples; the 2 pyproject.toml samples were
unchanged) diverged.

Locked decision (dispatcher directive 2026-05-01; Path A clean-
closure recommended by M7-partition-fix dispatch agent + locked
by main session per autonomy directive): recompute the 13 SHAs
on current HEAD, update the constants in
`framework/hands-off-lifecycle/tests/test_d1_byte_content_match.py`,
and add inline ODD §4 in-band retire-and-rebaseline comments
naming M8 (`6bef03b`) + AC.OSS.4 as the legitimate rebaseline
source.

Per `feedback_loose_AC_text_fix_AC_not_implementation` analog:
when implementation matches AC intent (Apache-header insertion
was the AC.OSS.4 directive) and the test's pinned bytes diverge
for a legitimate reason, rebaseline the test, not re-author the
impl. Same in-band rebaseline pattern as M-FBM applied for
primary-persona/__init__.py + session_start_emitter.py.

Structural remedy (single file edit):

  - `framework/hands-off-lifecycle/tests/test_d1_byte_content_match.py`
    — 13 SHA-256 constant updates + 13 inline narrative comments
    naming M8 + AC.OSS.4.

AC surface (AC.M8-corrective.1 + AC.M8-corrective.2 + AC.M8-corrective.S):

  - AC.M8-corrective.1: SHA-256 constants for the 13 .py samples
    match current bytes post-M8.
  - AC.M8-corrective.2: HOL's `test_d1_byte_content_match.py`
    passes 16/16 (13 rebaselined .py + 2 unchanged pyproject.toml
    + structural ≥15-samples check).
  - AC.M8-corrective.S: seal-diff invariant — only paths under
    `framework/hands-off-lifecycle/` + universal-paths.

Method-level choices (builder's call per ODD §1.1):

  - SHA recomputation tool (D1): Python `hashlib.sha256` against
    each file at current HEAD. Equivalent to `sha256sum`.
  - Comment style (D2): each rebaselined entry gains a
    per-constant inline comment naming M8 + the rebaseline
    reason (mirrors the M-FBM precedent shape on the same file).
  - Test scope (D3): narrow to HOL's `test_d1_byte_content_match.py`
    for pre-seal verification per `feedback_amendment_dispatch_speedups`.
    Cross-component seal-diff sweep at seal-time is sufficient.

Out of scope (per plan §8):

  - Re-running the M8 Apache-header script (M8 already executed
    it across 700 files; bytes are correct).
  - Re-baselining the 2 pyproject.toml samples (their bytes
    unchanged by M8; SHAs still match).
  - Edits to other HOL test files (only test_d1_byte_content_match.py
    is affected).
  - Touching M8's commit `6bef03b` (stays in audit trail; this
    corrective is an additive followup).

BASELINE `403bccd` (feature commit). HOL's SEAL_COMMIT sidecar
lands at the seal SHA via `loam amend seal`.

# M7-partition-fix — add docs/plugins/** glob to partition manifest

2026-05-01. Foldback for M11a dispatch-1 halt F-M11a.1 (synthesis
tool errors with `partition incomplete: 1 unclassified path(s);
samples: ['docs/plugins/dev-sdlc.md']`).

M7 commit `2fefd8b` ("docs(public): M7 plugins category — Dev/SDLC
plugin reference") added `docs/plugins/dev-sdlc.md` per M7 plan-doc
D-Q.M7.6 = (c) "separate `docs/plugins/<name>.md` category". M2's
partition manifest at
`framework/tools/pos-publish-framework-only/publish-mode-manifest.yaml`
was authored before M7 and never extended to admit the new
directory. M11a dispatch-1 fired §9.9 (synthesis tool errors on
partition incomplete) when run against `47cbea7`.

Locked decision (dispatcher directive 2026-05-01; no ambiguity):
add `- glob: "docs/plugins/**"` to the `dev_and_public:` block,
alongside the existing `docs/components/**` glob entry (around
line 157). Pre-flight verified `docs/plugins/dev-sdlc.md` carries
ZERO AC.OSS.3 residuals (pos-amend / loam-amend / A1-A4 /
loam-mode / docs/rebuild / pos-publish-framework-only /
odd-methodology / odd-in-loam / duration-estimation-rubric) and
ZERO AC.OSS.5 source-side residuals — public-plugin-reference is
clean for ship.

HOL is no-op narrative anchor only (per M2 + post-m6-partition-
realignment precedent) — sidecar bump + this notes file only;
no behaviour edits to HOL.

Structural remedy:

  - `framework/tools/pos-publish-framework-only/publish-mode-manifest.yaml`
    — add one glob entry under `dev_and_public:` (the new
    `docs/plugins/**` line + 6-line provenance comment).

AC surface (AC.M7-fix.1 + AC.M7-fix.2 + AC.M7-fix.S):

  - AC.M7-fix.1: partition manifest's `dev_and_public:` block
    contains `- glob: "docs/plugins/**"` alongside the existing
    `docs/components/**` glob.
  - AC.M7-fix.2: synthesis tool runs cleanly against post-fix HEAD
    (no `SynthesisError`, no `partition incomplete` error);
    `docs/plugins/dev-sdlc.md` appears in the synthesised tree.
  - AC.M7-fix.S: seal-diff invariant — only paths under
    `framework/tools/pos-publish-framework-only/` (structural) +
    `framework/hands-off-lifecycle/tests/SEAL_COMMIT*` (anchor) +
    universal-paths.

Method-level choices (builder's call per ODD §1.1):

  - Single-line glob entry under `dev_and_public:` (D1 locked by
    dispatcher; alternative shapes — per-plugin path entry, broader
    `docs/**` glob — rejected by directive).
  - HOL no-op anchor (D2 — convention per M2 precedent; tools-tree
    amendments need a sealed-component anchor since pos-publish-
    framework-only carries no test_no_sealed_amendments.py).
  - Synthesis smoke check post-fix (sanity test, not part of
    M11a's full sweep — that's M11a-2's job on re-dispatch).

Out of scope (per plan §8):

  - The full M11a sweep (AC.M11a.1..6) — re-dispatches against
    post-fix HEAD per D-Q.M11.4.
  - Other partition gaps that may surface during M11a-2 — separate
    corrective amendments.
  - Retroactive M7 plan-doc edits (M7 D-Q.M7.6 ruling was correct;
    omission was at M2-manifest-extension-time).
  - `docs/plugins/<future-plugin>.md` entries (the glob admits
    future additions under the same pattern).

BASELINE `b1dc662` (current HEAD; post-M11a-halt §14 commit). The
HOL anchor's SEAL_COMMIT sidecar lands at the seal SHA via
`loam amend seal`.

# C1 — Classes A+B partition reclassification

2026-05-02. Foldback for M11a dispatch-2 halt at AC.M11a.2 (three
named classes of public-tree dev-discipline-machinery residuals
surfaced by the M11a sweep). C1 closes Classes A + B; C2 (separate
sealed-component cycle, lands next) closes Class C.

Source surfaces (audit trail):

  - M11a dispatch-2 sweep report (per-file detail) at
    `<workspace>/.scratch/claude-output/oss-v0-1-0-publish-m11a-
    sweep-report.md`.
  - M11 plan-doc D-Q.M11.4 (always halt-and-surface; no
    auto-foldback at M11a; foldback amendments authored sealed
    before re-dispatch).
  - C1+C2 combined sub-plan at `docs/rebuild/plans/
    oss-v0-1-0-publish-public-docs-classes-abc.md`.
  - M7-partition-fix precedent (small-scope sealed-cycle + HOL
    no-op anchor): `docs/rebuild/plans/oss-v0-1-0-publish-public-
    docs-partition-fix.md`.

Locked decisions (plan §11; all 5 baked per autonomy directive):

  - D-Q.ABC.2 (Class A glob shape) = (a) framework-wide
    `**/seals/**`; verified zero false-positive matches outside
    the seven per-component `seals/` dirs at plan-time.
  - D-Q.ABC.3 (Class B glob shape) = (a) targeted exact patterns
    (`**/tests/test_no_sealed_amendments.py` +
    `**/tests/test_AC_*_seal_diff_*.py`); precision avoids
    accidentally excluding legitimate public tests.

HOL is no-op narrative anchor only (per M2 + M7-partition-fix
precedent) — sidecar bump + this notes file only; no behaviour
edits to HOL.

Structural remedy:

  - `framework/tools/pos-publish-framework-only/publish-mode-
    manifest.yaml` — add three glob entries under `dev_only:`:
    `**/seals/**`, `**/tests/test_no_sealed_amendments.py`,
    `**/tests/test_AC_*_seal_diff_*.py` (with provenance comments
    citing this plan-doc + D-Q.ABC.2 + D-Q.ABC.3).

AC surface (AC.ABC-A.1 + AC.ABC-B.1 + AC.ABC-B.2 + AC.ABC-C1.S):

  - AC.ABC-A.1: post-fix synthesis output carries zero blobs under
    any `seals/` directory across the framework tree.
  - AC.ABC-B.1: post-fix synthesis output carries zero blobs
    matching `**/tests/test_no_sealed_amendments.py`.
  - AC.ABC-B.2: post-fix synthesis output carries zero blobs
    matching `**/tests/test_AC_*_seal_diff_*.py`.
  - AC.ABC-C1.S: seal-diff invariant — only paths under
    `framework/tools/pos-publish-framework-only/` (structural) +
    `framework/hands-off-lifecycle/tests/SEAL_COMMIT*` (anchor) +
    universal-paths.

Verification empirically performed pre-seal: synthesis CLI
advanced refs/heads/framework-only against the post-feature HEAD;
`git ls-tree -r refs/heads/framework-only | grep -E '/seals/'`
returns zero hits; `... | grep -E 'test_no_sealed_amendments\\.py'`
returns zero hits; `... | grep -E 'test_AC_.*_seal_diff'` returns
zero hits. AC.ABC-A.1 + AC.ABC-B.1 + AC.ABC-B.2 PASS.

Method-level choices (builder's call per ODD §1.1):

  - Three glob entries appended to existing `dev_only:` block
    (under the `test_AC_AG_*` / `test_AC_BAG_*` HOL gate-test
    block; structural co-location with existing dev_only test
